# What NOT to publish on vom-turnkey.vercel.app.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the whole folder, so anything living here that is not part
# of the PUBLIC explainer ends up at a public URL. The product's working surfaces are
# gated behind /os (served by api/os.js); the source that powers them must never be
# fetchable as a static file.
#
# Public surface = index.html + api/ (the gate + the OS it serves).

# The agent-side operating system: engine source, orchestrator skill, subagents,
# and the operator profile (the white-label rails). Distributed by licence, not by URL.
orchestrator

# A separate Vercel project (vom-client-hub.vercel.app) that happens to live in this
# folder. Its server source has no business being served from this host.
client-hub

# Operator tools that predate the /os convention — they are being folded into the
# gated OS. Until then they are not public.
launch-wizard.html
hub-setup-wizard.html

# Repo furniture
README.md
OS-SETUP.md
.gitignore
.git
